To bend at a discontinuity, a smooth kernel shortens its length scale everywhere, and more
data push it further. Duvenaud's cookbook calls this a classic sign of misspecification;
near the step the 95% band covered 72%.

Plain split conformal adds one quantile of the calibration residuals to every prediction.
Coverage is marginal, so on a problem with growing noise it was 100%, 95% and 82% by third;
normalized scores or CQR make the width adapt.
